---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Load test request files and collections against one target origin

Usage: rustman bench [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...
          Request files or folders: one iteration runs them in collection order (default: the current directory)

Options:
      --target <URL>
          The origin under load, scheme://host[:port]; the only one requests may go to (required)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --executor <EXECUTOR>
          constant-vus (default), ramping-vus or constant-arrival-rate

      --vus <N>
          Virtual users of constant-vus (default 1)

      --duration <DURATION>
          How long load runs: 30s (default), 2m, 500ms

      --iterations <N>
          Iterations in total across every VU, instead of a duration

      --think-time <TIME>
          Pause between a VU's iterations: 0 (default), 1s, or a uniform range such as 1s..3s

      --stage <DURATION:VUS>
          A ramping-vus stage, <duration>:<vus>, as in 30s:20 (repeatable; replaces rustman.toml [[bench.stages]])

      --rate <N>
          Iterations started per second by constant-arrival-rate

      --max-vus <N>
          VU pool of constant-arrival-rate (default 50)

      --data <FILE>
          Feed each iteration a row of a CSV or JSON file as variables

      --data-mode <MODE>
          sequential (default, one shared cursor), per-vu (VU n uses row n) or random

      --data-exhaust <WHEN>
          At the last row: recycle (default) or stop

      --secret-columns <A,B>
          Data columns whose values are secrets and are redacted in every output, besides those named like password, token, secret or api_key

      --allow-mutations
          Also allow POST, PUT and PATCH

      --allow-destructive
          Also allow DELETE (implies --allow-mutations; never against production)

      --production <HOST>
          Confirm a production target by repeating its exact host

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per request, replacing settings.timeout_ms

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates

      --threshold <EXPR>
          Fail the bench (exit 1) unless <metric><op><value> holds at the end, as in p95<300ms, error_rate<1% or file:login:p99<1s; a trailing ! stops the bench as soon as it is breached (repeatable)

      --report <FORMAT[=PATH]>
          Also write the report as json, html, markdown, junit or sarif, to a file or stdout, as in html=out/bench.html (repeatable)

      --viz
          Stream per-second metrics to the viz companion (rustman-viz); the bench runs the same without it

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
